# Committed generated code under the CI drift gate.
#
# One line per `buf generate` invocation:
#
#     <package dir, from the repo root> | <gen dir, from the package> | <buf generate arguments>
#
# A package may appear more than once: several of these directories are generated
# from more than one proto root, and every invocation writes into the same gen dir.
# `scripts/generated-code.sh` clears that directory before the first invocation, so
# the committed set is exactly what the listed invocations produce — a file no proto
# generates any more is drift, not a leftover.
#
# Only TypeScript is listed because only TypeScript is committed. The Rust bindings
# come from the `build.rs` passes in packages/tddy-service, which write into OUT_DIR
# on every build and therefore cannot drift; packages/tddy-service/src/gen holds a
# .gitkeep and nothing else.

packages/tddy-web                   | src/gen | ../tddy-service/proto
# `#unbundle` node 6 serves `terminal_session.TerminalSessionService` from tddy-terminal-rpc,
# whose proto lives outside tddy-service's tree. A second root, the way tddy-livekit-web
# already reaches tddy-service/proto for terminal.proto.
packages/tddy-web                   | src/gen | ../tddy-terminal-rpc/proto
packages/tddy-rpc-web               | src/gen | ../tddy-rpc/proto
packages/tddy-rpc-web               | src/gen | ../tddy-livekit/proto --path ../tddy-livekit/proto/test
packages/tddy-livekit-web           | src/gen | ../tddy-livekit/proto
packages/tddy-livekit-web           | src/gen | ../tddy-rpc/proto
packages/tddy-livekit-web           | src/gen | ../tddy-service/proto --path ../tddy-service/proto/terminal.proto
packages/tddy-rust-typescript-tests | gen     | ../tddy-service/proto
